    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0506" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d168-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-16">16/7/43</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 366. Former Naval Person to President
                    personal and secret.</p>
                <p>I like very much the plan of our meeting in Canada and think the <pb facs="0507"
                        n="393" xml:id="pg393"/> Heights of Abraham most attractive. We think it most important to have the
                    meeting earlier than September 1. The Combined Staffs at Washington agreed to
                    meet again at the end of July or the beginning of August. We could come with our
                    outfit by the same method as last time arriving at the very spot between the
                    12th and 15th of August. If this is agreeable to you, I will open the matter to
                    Mackenzie King in the greatest secrecy.</p>
                <p>Events in 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Husky</hi>
                     are moving so fast and the degeneration of Italian resistance is so
                    marked that decisions about the Toe, Ball and Heel, which were regarded as a
                    part of 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Husky</hi>, will almost certainly have
                    to be taken before we meet. We shall, however, need to meet together to settle
                    the larger issues which the brilliant victories of our Forces are thrusting upon
                    us about Italy as a whole. Mid-August will only just be in time for this work.
                    This, also, will be the time to check up intimately upon de Gaulle, UJ and other equally agreeable topics. I hope,
                    therefore, that you will be able to give me this date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prime</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
